{"schema": 1, "kind": "review", "id": "rev-20261123T180933Z-aeef66b5", "ts": "2026-11-23T18:12:11Z", "actor": {"worktree": "prawduct", "plugin": "3.9.1-dev", "branch": "fix/stop-final-nudge", "build": "e1b8ea002110"}, "body": {"base_commit": "b123a8119ae34e87c6bbf50b4982439d90f25cc0", "base_tree": "7dca4821ee6dd3b729e6457e139ab7d1cbba6dd7", "head_tree": "10cd834967a7c69ca1ffeab77a78276eeb30dbf5", "head_commit": "fdddecb60a46b9415fad6201b466a2c4f90b0ffc", "dispatch_commit": "fdddecb60a46b9415fad6201b466a2c4f90b0ffc", "mode": "cumulative (bundle review, ready for merge)", "mode_chosen_by": "rule-2 cumulative: branch is 4 commits ahead of origin/develop, working tree clean, no fresh cumulative-mode record for current HEAD, and no composed review coverage spans the branch", "stage": "boundary", "tier": "escalate", "roster": [{"role": "correctness", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, {"role": "design", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, {"role": "sustainability", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}], "files_reviewed": ["plugin/bin/prawduct-hook", "plugin/lib/gates.py", "tests/test_critic_gate_fallthrough.py", "tests/test_session_critic_gate.py"], "files_changed": [".prawduct/changes/stop-final-nudge.md", ".prawduct/owner-rulings.md", "plugin/bin/prawduct-hook", "plugin/lib/gates.py", "tests/test_critic_gate_fallthrough.py", "tests/test_session_critic_gate.py"], "files_oracle": [".prawduct/changes/stop-final-nudge.md", ".prawduct/owner-rulings.md"], "findings": [], "counts": {"blocking": 0, "warning": 0, "note": 0}, "observations": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "The walk picks the newest review at the pass's base tree, which is not always the review the pass anchored to", "recommendation": "No change needed for this fix. `coverage_algebra.prior_review` matches on tree equality across the whole store and returns the newest review standing at the verify pass's `base_tree`. When several reviews stand at that tree with different modes, that newest one need not be the anchor `critic_consolidate._prior_review_fact` chose, and the advisory's answer could differ from what the pass actually verified. A read of the live store found this tie in 11 of 867 verify passes, with mixed non-verify modes in only 1. The rule has one owner and `carried_blocking` reads it the same way, so the two cannot disagree. If it ever matters, the fix belongs in that owner: record the anchor id on the verify fact and follow it. Don't patch this advisory.", "files": ["plugin/lib/gates.py"], "oid": "O-1"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "The 'not a sibling's newer review steering this one' claim holds only while no other worktree records a review at the same tree", "recommendation": "The walk runs over the whole store, and coverage_algebra.prior_review picks the NEWEST review whose head_tree equals the pass's base_tree. If another worktree later records a review (say a `chunk`) at that identical tree, the pass here resolves to that review, and the advisory flips. That is exactly the steering the new comment in _critic_session_satisfies_gate says cannot happen. It is rare, because it needs two worktrees reviewing a byte-identical tree. It is advisory-only, and it matches the hop carried_blocking takes, so no edit is wanted unless this shows up in practice. If it does, the fix is instance-scoped: when several reviews stand at the base tree, prefer the one from this worktree.", "files": ["plugin/lib/gates.py"], "oid": "O-2"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "title": "Test docstrings cite 'Case (a)', 'Case (b)' and 'Case (c)', which nothing in the tree defines", "recommendation": "The docstring on _critic_session_satisfies_gate numbers its cases 0-7. The new tests in TestSynthesisAdvisoryWalksBackOverVerifyPasses cite lettered cases from the builder's working notes, so a reader cannot resolve them. Nothing reads these docstrings, so this is wording only. If the file is touched again, drop the letters or use the docstring's numbers (6 and 7). Instance.", "files": ["tests/test_critic_gate_fallthrough.py"], "oid": "O-3"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "_append_review_at's other-worktree branch repeats _append_foreign_review's raw fact writer in the same file", "recommendation": "Both helpers hand-write the same schema/kind/id/ts/actor JSON line to evidence.store_path. They differ only in id, the body's trees and the timestamp. Adding base/head keyword arguments to _append_foreign_review, and calling it from _append_review_at, would leave one copy of the store-line shape in this test module. It is small test-only duplication, so no edit is owed. Instance.", "files": ["tests/test_critic_gate_fallthrough.py"], "oid": "O-4"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "Framework-Specific Checks not applicable", "recommendation": "The diff touches no skill, template, methodology or Critic-protocol file. It changes gate code, a hook comment and tests only, so Generality, Instruction Clarity, Cumulative Health and Pipeline Coverage do not apply. No edit wanted.", "oid": "O-5"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "title": "Renumbering the advisory's case list left test citations pointing at the old cases and at letters the docstring never had", "recommendation": "Class: these comments cite a case by its position in a numbered docstring list, and inserting a case shifts every position. Search tests/ and plugin/lib for '_critic_session_satisfies_gate case' and 'Case ('. At tests/test_critic_gate_fallthrough.py:209 the helper still cites 'case 4/5'. Before this change that meant chunk-unsatisfied / final-satisfied; now case 4 is 'no review' and the chunk case is 6. The new tests at :542, :558, :582 and :598 cite 'Case (a)' and 'Case (c)', and the docstring (cases 0-7) has no lettered cases. Name each case by its condition (for example 'the chunk-under-a-pass case') instead of its number, or delete the citation. Nothing reads these comments, so this is an observation and no fix round is wanted.", "files": ["tests/test_critic_gate_fallthrough.py", "plugin/lib/gates.py"], "oid": "O-6"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "title": "New docstrings narrate the defect's history", "recommendation": "Instance. The _critic_session_satisfies_gate docstring ends with 'Read off the pass itself, every clean close ... drew a nudge to run a final nobody owed'. The test docstrings say '(seen four times on 2026-11-23)' and 'reported as that printed line (2026-11-23)'. Each says what used to happen rather than what the code does. The relational half ('a pass does not undo the synthesis of the review it verifies') already carries the reason, so the history clause can be deleted the next time these lines are touched. Inert prose, and no edit is wanted now.", "files": ["plugin/lib/gates.py", "tests/test_critic_gate_fallthrough.py", "tests/test_session_critic_gate.py"], "oid": "O-7"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "title": "Records Pass: the consumer note uses the store-position wording the fragment body rejects, and leaves out the unlinked-pass case", "recommendation": "Records Pass, below every bar. The consumer note says 'The NOTE still appears when the last review before your verify pass was a chunk'. The body says the walk follows the recorded link, 'not by store position', and the NOTE also fires for a pass that links to no review. In the ordinary single-session flow the two readings agree, and verify_anchor builds the link by construction, so no consumer acts wrongly on it. If the fragment is edited anyway, 'the review your verify pass verifies' is the accurate wording. Separately, 'Tests pin each case on the predicate and on the Stop hook's printed advisories' is true of the predicate. The Stop-hook pins cover two cases (cumulative+verify, chunk+verify). Neither claim clears a bar.", "files": [".prawduct/changes/stop-final-nudge.md"], "oid": "O-8"}], "duration_seconds": 420, "scope": null, "scope_chosen_by": "none", "scope_unresolved_cause": "unbound", "scope_reason": "no live plan claims 